  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COMMUNITY CONSERVATION OF LEATHERBACK TURTLES IN PLAYA CHACAHUA SANCTUARY, OAXACA, MEXICO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PLAYA CHACAHUA SANCTUARY (PCS) IN OAXACA, MEXICO (1602 39.75N 9752 58.42W - 1557 12.61N 9728 39.72W) IS A FEDERAL PROTECTED AREA. IT INCLUDES FOUR BEACHES OF GREAT IMPORTANCE FOR NESTING LEATHERBACK TURTLES: LA TUZA, SAN JUAN, BAHA DE CHACAHUA AND CERRO HERMOSO, WHICH TOTAL 30.3 MILES AND IN WHICH AROUND 85 NESTS ARE REGISTERED ANNUALLY. THE SANCTUARY IS ADMINISTERED BY THE NATIONAL COMMISSION OF PROTECTED NATURAL AREAS.THE MAIN THREATS TO LEATHERBACK TURTLES IN THE PCS INCLUDE THE ILLEGAL POACHING OF EGGS FOR COMMERCIAL PURPOSES AND FOR LOCAL CONSUMPTION THE IMPACT OF CLIMATE CHANGE ON NESTS PREDATION BY DOGS AND POOR VISITATION PRACTICES.ALTHOUGH THE PCS HAS A MONITORING PROGRAM THAT INVOLVES THE PARTICIPATION OF MEMBERS OF FIVE COMMUNITY SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION CAMPS, THE FINANCIAL RESOURCES ALLOCATED FOR THIS PROGRAM ARE INSUFFICIENT TO ACHIEVE EFFECTIVE PROTECTION OF ALL NESTS AND TO GENERATE UPDATED INFORMATION ON THE POPULATION OF LEATHERBACK TURTLES THAT NEST IN THE PCS.IN ORDER TO ADDRESS THESE THREATS, WILDCOAST AND THE PCS ARE COLLABORATING TO CARRY OUT THE PROJECT COMMUNITY CONSERVATION OF LEATHERBACK TURTLES IN PLAYA CHACAHUA SANCTUARY, OAXACA, MEXICO. THE GOAL IS THAT IN THREE YEARS, ON THE BEACHES OF THE PLAYA CHACAHUA SANCTUARY, 100% OF THE LEATHERBACK TURTLES AND THEIR NESTS WILL BE MONIT</narrative>
  </description>
